---
title: Cacio E Pepe
description: Italian peppery-cheesy pasta
cuisine: Italian 
course: Main Dish
cook time: 10 minutes
servings: 2
prep time: 5 minutes
time required: 25 minutes
source: https://www.spoonforkbacon.com/cacio-e-pepe-recipe/
---

== Pasta == 

Fill a large #pot{} with water and bring to a boil over high heat.

Add a small handful of @salt{handful} and @pasta{8%oz} to boiling water.

Cook pasta, stirring occasionally until al dente, ~{6 to 8%minutes}.

Drain pasta, reserving 2/3 cup pasta water.

> Note: Don't skip reserving the pasta water! The starch is key to giving the sauce its creamy consistency!

Pour pasta back into pot or into a large skillet and place over low heat.


== Sauce ==

Add pasta water and @butter{2%tbsp} and toss together until butter just melts.

Add @freshly grated Pecorino Romano{1/2%cup} and @black pepper{1/2%tsp} and continue to toss together until cheese melts and a creamy sauce forms.

Top with more grated cheese and serve.

